        <li><strong>Phase 3: User-Centric Testing.</strong> Workshops with individuals with varying disabilities (visual, auditory, motor, and cognitive) to validate the adaptive nature of the proposed interface.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Expected Outcomes</h2>
    <p>
        Upon completion, this project aims to deliver a robust toolkit and a legislative recommendation for public officials, utilizing the rigorous discipline of a <em>constable</em> applied to ethical design standards. We aim to demonstrate that accessible technology is not a cost, but a fundamental right that improves quality of life for all citizens.
    </p>

    <div class="signature">
        <p>Dr. A. S. Wright</p>
        <p>Lead Researcher</p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
```

